{
  "id": "11",
  "title": "Prism Templates",
  "content": "<div style=\"background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(99, 102, 241, 0.12) 0%, rgba(139, 92, 246, 0.04) 100%); border: 1px solid rgba(99, 102, 241, 0.2); border-left: 4px solid #6366F1; padding: 32px; margin-bottom: 60px; border-radius: 4px; position: relative; overflow: hidden;\"><div style=\"position: absolute; top: -20px; right: -20px; opacity: 0.1; transform: rotate(15deg);\"><svg width=\"120\" height=\"120\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6366F1\" stroke-width=\"1\"><path d=\"M12 2L2 7l10 5 10-5-10-5z\"/><path d=\"M2 17l10 5 10-5\"/><path d=\"M2 12l10 5 10-5\"/></svg></div><p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 20px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--text-heading); font-weight: 300;\"><strong>Prism</strong> is Photon's high-performance refraction engine. Inspired by Laravel's Blade, it compiles expressive templates into raw JavaScript closures for near-instant rendering.</p></div><h2>The View Compiler</h2><p>Unlike traditional template engines that parse strings at runtime, Prism utilizes an <strong>AOT (Ahead-of-Time) View Compiler</strong>. Your HTML is strictly analyzed and transformed into optimized execution paths during the boot phase.</p><div style=\"display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 24px; margin: 48px 0;\" class=\"bento-grid\"><div style=\"background: var(--surf-bg); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding: 32px; border-radius: 4px; transition: all 0.3s ease;\" onmouseover=\"this.style.borderColor='rgba(99,102,241,0.4)'; this.style.transform='translateY(-4px)'\" onmouseout=\"this.style.borderColor='var(--border-subtle)'; this.style.transform='translateY(0)'\"> <div style=\"color: #6366F1; margin-bottom: 20px;\"><svg width=\"32\" height=\"32\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"16 18 22 12 16 6\"/><polyline points=\"8 6 2 12 8 18\"/></svg></div><h3 style=\"margin: 0 0 12px 0; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 800; tracking: 0.05em; border: none; padding: 0;\">LOGIC_DRIVEN</h3><p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 14px; opacity: 0.8; padding: 0; border: none;\">Full support for conditional directives (<code>@if</code>) and iterative loops (<code>@each</code>) without context switching overhead.</p></div><div style=\"background: var(--surf-bg); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding: 32px; border-radius: 4px; transition: all 0.3s ease;\" onmouseover=\"this.style.borderColor='rgba(99,102,241,0.4)'; this.style.transform='translateY(-4px)'\" onmouseout=\"this.style.borderColor='var(--border-subtle)'; this.style.transform='translateY(0)'\"><div style=\"color: #6366F1; margin-bottom: 20px;\"><svg width=\"32\" height=\"32\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"3\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\" ry=\"2\"/><line x1=\"3\" y1=\"9\" x2=\"21\" y2=\"9\"/><line x1=\"9\" y1=\"21\" x2=\"9\" y2=\"9\"/></svg></div><h3 style=\"margin: 0 0 12px 0; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 800; tracking: 0.05em; border: none; padding: 0;\">SLOT_SYSTEM</h3><p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 14px; opacity: 0.8; padding: 0; border: none;\">Powerful component architecture with named slots and props, enabling deep dry-principle UI composition.</p></div><div style=\"background: var(--surf-bg); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding: 32px; border-radius: 4px; transition: all 0.3s ease;\" onmouseover=\"this.style.borderColor='rgba(99,102,241,0.4)'; this.style.transform='translateY(-4px)'\" onmouseout=\"this.style.borderColor='var(--border-subtle)'; this.style.transform='translateY(0)'\"><div style=\"color: #6366F1; margin-bottom: 20px;\"><svg width=\"32\" height=\"32\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M21 15v4a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-4\"/><polyline points=\"7 10 12 15 17 10\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"15\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"3\"/></svg></div><h3 style=\"margin: 0 0 12px 0; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 800; tracking: 0.05em; border: none; padding: 0;\">STACK_MGMT</h3><p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 14px; opacity: 0.8; padding: 0; border: none;\">Push scripts and styles from nested views into the master layout without breaking the document structure.</p></div></div><h2>Refracted Syntax</h2><p>Prism syntax is designed to be readable and expressive. It combines the simplicity of curly braces with the power of Laravel-style directives.</p><pre><code>@extends('layouts/app')\n\n@section('content')\n  &lt;h1&gt;Hello, {{ user.name }}&lt;/h1&gt;\n  \n  &lt;x-alert type=\"success\"&gt;\n    Your profile has been updated.\n  &lt;/x-alert&gt;\n\n  &lt;ul&gt;\n    {{#each items as item}}\n      &lt;li&gt;{{ item.title }}&lt;/li&gt;\n    {{/each}}\n  &lt;/ul&gt;\n@endsection</code></pre><div style=\"background: rgba(99, 102, 241, 0.05); border: 1px solid rgba(99, 102, 241, 0.1); border-left: 4px solid #6366F1; padding: 24px; margin: 40px 0; border-radius: 0 4px 4px 0;\"><h4 style=\"margin: 0 0 10px 0; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 900; color: #6366F1; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em;\">// COMPILER_SPEC: STRING_ELIMINATION</h4><p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 15px; font-style: italic; color: var(--text-heading); opacity: 0.9; border: none; padding: 0;\">Literal strings in your templates are pre-concatenated during compilation. The resulting JS function performs a single <code>return</code> of the pre-built buffer, minimizing intermediate string allocation.</p></div><h2>Performance Benchmark</h2><p>Rendering overhead comparison: Prism (AOT) vs Traditional String-Replace Enginess (10k simple renders).</p><div style=\"background: var(--surf-bg); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding: 32px; margin: 40px 0; border-radius: 4px;\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 24px;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 800; color: #6366F1; margin-bottom: 12px; font-family: var(--font-technical);\"><span>PRISM_AOT_RENDER</span> <span>0.004ms AVG</span></div><div style=\"height: 8px; background: rgba(99,102,241,0.1); width: 100%; border-radius: 4px; overflow: hidden;\"><div style=\"height: 100%; width: 10%; background: #6366F1; box-shadow: 0 0 15px rgba(99,102,241,0.5);\"></div></div></div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 0;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 800; color: #6B7280; margin-bottom: 12px; font-family: var(--font-technical);\"><span>GENERIC_SSR_ENGINE</span> <span>0.210ms AVG</span></div><div style=\"height: 8px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.05); width: 100%; border-radius: 4px; overflow: hidden;\"><div style=\"height: 100%; width: 85%; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.2);\"></div></div></div><p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; font-family: var(--font-technical); border: none; padding: 0;\">// METRIC: AOT COMPILATION REDUCES VIEW LATENCY BY OVER 50X</p></div><h2>Hypermedia Hybridization</h2><p>Prism is the perfect partner for <strong>HTMX</strong>. It allows you to return granular HTML fragments that feel as fast as a client-side SPA without the bloat of a JavaScript bundle.</p><pre><code>// Return only the list fragment for HTMX swapping\napp.get('/api/users', (c) => {\n  const view = c.get('view')\n  return c.html(view.render('partials/user-list'))\n})</code></pre><div style=\"background: linear-gradient(to right, rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.1), transparent); border-left: 4px solid #10B981; padding: 24px; margin-top: 60px; border-radius: 0 4px 4px 0;\"><p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 500; font-style: italic; border: none; padding: 0; color: var(--text-heading);\">**Architect's Insight:** Prism is not just a templating engine; it's a bridge between the reliability of Server-Side Rendering and the interactivity of modern web standards. Use it for high-concurrency applications where performance is non-negotiable.</p></div>",
